// df.d.ts state BEFORE e1 (substrate-on).
//
// At episode-1 boot, the substrate-on arm has:
//   - the per_entity seed at <baseDir>/lib/__seed__/per_entity.ts
//   - empty per-tenant lib at <baseDir>/lib/productflow-jsonplaceholder/
//
// The df.d.ts manifest at this point declares ONLY:
//   - the substrate boilerplate types (Result, AnswerEnvelope, etc.)
//   - the 5 jsonplaceholder tool primitives under df.tool.jsonplaceholder.*
//   - the per_entity seed under df.lib.per_entity
//
// It does NOT yet declare any learned df.lib.* — those crystallise after e2.
//
// To inspect the EXACT pre-e1 manifest, run:
//   rm -rf eval/productFlow/results/p2-substrate-on-20260517-fresh
//   pnpm tsx src/eval/productFlow/runProductFlowMicroEval.ts \
//     --arm substrate-on --task e1 --dry-run \
//     --out-dir eval/productFlow/results/p2-substrate-on-20260517-fresh
//   cat eval/productFlow/results/p2-substrate-on-20260517-fresh/datafetch-home/df.d.ts
//
// (the --dry-run path renders the manifest as it would be seen by the
// agent without spending a Claude call).
